Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.git
.gitignore
*.md
# We don't want to ignore dist in the builder stage, it's created there.
# coverage is a test artifact, not needed in image.
coverage
# .env files should typically not be copied into images for security.
# Environment variables should be injected at runtime.
.env
# Exclude TypeScript source files from the final production image if only JS is run
# However, the current Dockerfile copies all source with COPY . . in the builder stage
# and then only copies the dist folder to the production stage.
# So, explicitly ignoring src here is not strictly necessary for the final image size
# but can speed up the initial COPY . . if src is large.
# src # Optional: uncomment if you want to ensure src is not copied in initial COPY . . 